{
 "format": "notice-coverage-review/1",
 "statement": "A statement of what the reviewer of the change examined, bound to exact content: the curated inputs (the supplier component table; the coverage inputs: owner readings, permitted texts, Library content, icon provenance, stated removals), the indexes that generators make from caches CI does not hold, and the declared pin's distribution record, whose digests the account copies. The reviewer reruns the cache-reading checks for a changed index. It is not a proof: the checks are operator-run on stable inputs, and the record's truth rests on the review of the pull request that changes it, not on the tool. A supplier pin move changes which distribution record is bound, so it updates this record in the same change.",
 "updated_by": "The independent reviewer of the pull request that changes any file listed here, after reviewing that change.",
 "reviewed_in": "pull request 243: review round 3 confirmed the 33 supplier rows for 0.167.0 and round 4 the bound digests; PR 238 (merged) carried the declared pin 0.169.0's distribution record. Proposed in the 0.169.0 supplier-notices change, pending an independent reading and not yet reviewed: components.json re-associated to 0.169.0 from the supplier's source at d32063f9 and the distribution record (36 rows; the voice rows open because sources.json changed; three new open rows: the imagegen and openai-docs skill samples and the vendored bubblewrap), the two LLVM CREDITS texts, the also_at identities, and the crate group (supplier_notices/crates/associations.json and index.json, with the two lockfiles bound through associations.json) covering every package of both lockfiles, with 138 gaps and 5 packages awaiting an owner reading open. Pull request 389 (the held-evidence change): its independent reviews examined the whole change, the two notice READMEs and the checkers' standing sites and tests. For the 53 Codex crates newly standing text and the 18 objc2 crates newly held, each locked archive was verified against its lockfile checksum and only its VCS record and manifest read; their repository, revision and package identity, the selected publisher texts' blobs and sizes in the saved listings, and the stored bytes were compared for every one (three archives state no package path; their recorded basis was read against the listings). The six crates recorded absent from the macOS target were verified against the five committed parent manifests, the three registry manifests against their checksum-verified archives and the two workspace manifests against the saved pinned reads and source listing, with the rule that admitted each workspace parent. The two voice records were compared with the declared pin's distribution record, and the nine voice rows' versions, source URLs, members and licence files with those records and with the 0.167.0 inventory reviewed in pull request 243. The eight no-publisher-text rows and the 53 remaining gaps were read for their stated facts. The nine bound digests and the generated accounts were verified. Not examined: the supplier's distribution archive and the content of the voice licence files inside it, the supplier's build files that say which executable is built from which lockfile, the workspace root manifest, and a rebuild of the archive-derived index. No licence adequacy question was decided; those remain the owner's.",
